{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "c9f2d4ab-reject-matrix-0001",
		"name": "SignFlow Rejection Matrix",
		"description": "Exercises every server-side rejection path of the coordination API.\n\nONE DOCUMENT, ONE SIGNER: the account that uploads a document is the account that signs it. There is no signing order and no turn to claim, so a second account is not a participant waiting its turn — it is a stranger, and the server answers it the same way it answers a document id that never existed.\n\nSETUP FIRST (one command, server must already be running):\n  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File postman/setup-rejection-matrix.ps1\n\nIt creates a dedicated single-signer workflow with alice's certificate bound at creation (so revision 0 exists and can be signed against), downloads revision 0, builds the tampered fixtures and writes fixtures/matrix-env.json. Import that as a Postman ENVIRONMENT and select it.\n\nSET THE WORKING DIRECTORY: the file fields below are relative paths like fixtures/rev0.pdf, so point Postman at this folder — Settings > General > Working directory > the repository's postman/ folder. (They used to be absolute paths on one developer's machine, which nobody else could run.)\n\nThen run the collection top to bottom: every request asserts its exact expected status code AND error code, so the whole suite should show green. Requests that do not override auth inherit alice's bearer token from section 0; the ones that must not use it say so with 'noauth' and carry their own header.\n\nWhat is covered: JWT enforcement, the uniform 404 that hides a document from everyone it does not belong to (on read AND write routes), stale parent revision, stale parent hash, byte-prefix tampering, chain-breaking append, unsigned resubmission, fingerprint validation, enrolling a certificate for somebody else, idempotency replay. NOT covered from raw HTTP: a cryptographically valid signature from a DIFFERENT certificate (needs the desktop app's PKCS#11 signing - see the 'Wrong certificate' request's description for the manual repro).",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "bearer",
		"bearer": [
			{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }
		]
	},
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
		{ "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "workflowId", "value": "SET_BY_SETUP_SCRIPT" },
		{ "key": "parentRevision", "value": "0" },
		{ "key": "parentSha256", "value": "SET_BY_SETUP_SCRIPT" },
		{ "key": "operationId", "value": "SET_BY_SETUP_SCRIPT" }
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "0. Auth",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Login (alice)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"login 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", json.accessToken);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", json.refreshToken);",
									"pm.test(\"tokens saved\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(json.accessToken).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty;",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"alice\",\n  \"password\": \"alice-pass\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "No token -> 401",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"401 without credentials\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
									"pm.test(\"structured JSON error\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"UNAUTHORIZED\");",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/my-tasks",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "workflows", "my-tasks"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Garbage token -> 401",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"401 for garbage bearer\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer not.a.real.jwt" }
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/my-tasks",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "workflows", "my-tasks"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "1. Authorization",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Login (charlie)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"login 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"charlieToken\", json.accessToken);",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", json.refreshToken);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"charlie\",\n  \"password\": \"charlie-pass\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Outsider reads workflow -> 404",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"404 for anyone it is not\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
									"pm.test(\"WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND — the uniform answer\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND\");",
									"});",
									"// Deliberately indistinguishable from a workflow id that never",
									"// existed: a 403 would confirm that this id IS a real document,",
									"// which is a disclosure in itself. requireAccessible answers the",
									"// same 404 to a stranger and to a typo."
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{charlieToken}}" }
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "workflows", "{{workflowId}}"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Outsider downloads document -> 404",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"404 for anyone it is not\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
									"pm.test(\"WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND\");",
									"});",
									"// Same answer on the bytes route as on the metadata route: the",
									"// 404 is applied by requireAccessible before any state is read,",
									"// so no route leaks what the others conceal."
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{charlieToken}}" }
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/document",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "workflows", "{{workflowId}}", "document"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "2. Not the signer (a second account on a write route)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Login (bob)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
								"pm.test(\"login bob 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
								"const json = pm.response.json();",
								"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"bobToken\", json.accessToken);",
								"pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", json.refreshToken);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"bob\",\n  \"password\": \"bob-pass\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Bob downloads document -> 404",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"404, not 409\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
									"pm.test(\"WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND\");",
									"});",
									"// This used to be 409 NOT_YOUR_TURN, when bob held slot 2 of a",
									"// two-signer workflow and was waiting his turn. A document has",
									"// exactly one signer now, so bob is not a participant at all and",
									"// gets the same uniform 404 as any stranger."
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{bobToken}}" }
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/document",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "workflows", "{{workflowId}}", "document"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Bob submits a signature -> 404",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"404 before any content check\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
									"pm.test(\"WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND\", () => {",
									"    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql(\"WORKFLOW_NOT_FOUND\");",
									"});",
									"// The point of this case survives the single-signer change: the",
									"// access gate still fires BEFORE the PDF is looked at, so a",
									"// stranger cannot learn anything about the document by submitting",
									"// bytes at it. Only the reason changed, from a turn to ownership."
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": { "type": "noauth" },
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{bobToken}}" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "formdata",
							"formdata": [
								{
									"key": "request",
									"type": "text",
									"value": "{\"parentRevision\":{{parentRevision}},\"parentSha256\":\"{{parentSha256}}\",\"signingOperationId\":\"bob-out-of-turn-attempt\"}"
								},
								{
									"key": "file",
									"type": "file",
									"src": "fixtures/rev0.pdf"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}/signatures",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "workflows", "{{workflowId}}", "signatures"]
						}
					},
					"response": []
				}
			]
		},
